{"t": 1785378359.0, "lenguaje": "html", "temperature": 0.2, "reasoning_effort": null, "max_tokens": null, "system": "You are a creative front-end developer. Write complete, self-contained HTML pages with inline CSS and JavaScript and no external resources. The page must animate by itself on load. Follow the output format exactly.", "prompt": "You are a creative front-end developer making self-contained web pages.\n\nWrite a complete HTML page for: **Un carrito de compra con STOCK en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 3 productos como <div class=\"prod\"> con data-id p1,p2,p3, data-precio 100,50,25 y data-stock 2,3,1. Cada uno tiene un <button class=\"add\" data-id=\"pX\">. El carrito muestra sus lineas como <div class=\"linea\"> con data-id, cada una con <span class=\"cant\"> y un <button class=\"quitar\" data-id=\"pX\">. <span id=\"total\"> tiene el total. REGLAS: anadir el mismo producto NO crea una linea nueva, incrementa su cantidad. NO se puede superar el stock: al llegar al tope, el boton add de ESE producto queda disabled. Al quitar una unidad, si la cantidad llega a 0 la linea DESAPARECE y el boton add vuelve a habilitarse. El total se recalcula siempre.. TARGET LOOK, match it: A clean, single-page layout with a vertical split: the left side displays three product cards stacked, each with a bold price and a small “Add” button, while the right side hosts the cart panel with a header, list of line items (each showing product id, quantity, and a remove button), and a total at the bottom. The visual hierarchy emphasizes the cart totals and actions, using a muted teal‑gray palette with contrasting teal accents for buttons, and a modern sans‑serif font for clarity.**\n\nCRITICAL RULES — all must be followed:\n- ONE single self-contained .html file\n- Inline <style> and <script> — no external files\n- NO external resources: no CDN, no <link href=http...>, no fetch(), no remote images or fonts. It must work fully offline.\n- Implement EXACTLY the behavior the idea specifies. Nothing happens on its own: NO setInterval animations and NO random data unless the idea explicitly asks for them.\n- The INITIAL state must match the idea exactly (e.g. a counter that starts at 0 shows 0 and only changes on user action).\n- Reproduce LITERALLY every id=, class= and element the idea marks as required: automated tests will query those exact selectors.\n- Draw charts as inline <svg> — NOT <canvas>, and never a chart library\n- Responsive and legible on a phone screen\n- If you color-code state (up/down, green/red), put the state class on the SAME element your CSS selector targets. A rule like `.row.up span` only works if the class lands on `.row`, not on the inner span.\n- Set colors with a rule that matches the element you actually modify, and prefer setting style/class on the element you create in JS\n- Write ALL visible text in the SAME language as the page topic above\n- If you use <canvas>: set canvas.width = canvas.clientWidth and canvas.height = canvas.clientHeight BEFORE drawing, and redraw on resize. A canvas stretched by CSS from its default 300x150 renders squashed and blurry. Inline <svg> avoids this entirely and is preferred\n- Format numbers for humans: thousands separators, 2 decimals, currency symbol where money (toLocaleString)\n- Render a complete first frame IMMEDIATELY on load — never a blank page waiting for the first setInterval tick\n- REQUIRED component 1: Un carrito de compra con STOCK en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 3 productos como <div class=\"prod\"> con data-id p1\n- REQUIRED component 2: data-precio 100\n- REQUIRED component 3: data-stock 2\n- REQUIRED component 4: 1. Cada uno tiene un <button class=\"add\" data-id=\"pX\">. El carrito muestra sus lineas como <div class=\"linea\"> con data-id\n- REQUIRED component 5: cada una con <span class=\"cant\">\n- REQUIRED component 6: un <button class=\"quitar\" data-id=\"pX\">. <span id=\"total\"> tiene el total. REGLAS: anadir el mismo producto NO crea una linea nueva\n- REQUIRED component 7: incrementa su cantidad. NO se puede superar el stock: al llegar al tope\n- REQUIRED component 8: el boton add de ESE producto queda disabled. Al quitar una unidad\n- REQUIRED component 9: si la cantidad llega a 0 la linea DESAPARECE\n- REQUIRED component 10: el boton add vuelve a habilitarse. El total se recalcula siempre.. TARGET LOOK\n- Implement EVERY required component above — a page that skips any of them is WRONG. Prefer a LONGER page over an incomplete one; there is no size limit.\n- Demonstrate itself with built-in sample data and print results.\n\nPROVEN PATTERNS from pages that already passed browser checks and professional review. ADAPT their techniques to this idea — do NOT copy them verbatim; change data, labels, colors and layout to fit:\n--- tiles_kpi ---\n<!-- PATRON: fila de tiles KPI para la cabecera de un dashboard.\n     Por que funciona: los numeros grandes arriba dan jerarquia visual (algo\n     domina la vista); el delta con flecha + color nunca comunica por color\n     solo; grid auto-fit lo hace responsive sin media queries. -->\n<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:12px\">\n  <div style=\"background:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:12px;color:#52514e\">Valor de la cartera</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:26px;font-weight:650\" id=\"kpi-total\">14.324,53 €</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:13px;color:#006300\" id=\"kpi-delta\">▲ +171,93 € desde apertura</div>\n    <!-- si baja: color:#d03b3b y flecha ▼ — SIEMPRE flecha + color, no color solo -->\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n--- grafico_svg ---\n<!-- PATRON: grafico de linea SVG con ejes y escala segura.\n     Por que funciona: <text> en el eje Y (sin etiquetas no se sabe que\n     numeros muestra); la escala se calcula de los datos con RANGO MINIMO\n     (sin el, min==max en el primer tick da division por cero y los\n     atributos salen NaN — error real medido); rejilla fina y recesiva. -->\n<svg id=\"grafico\" width=\"100%\" height=\"220\" viewBox=\"0 0 600 220\"></svg>\n<script>\nfunction pintar(datos) {                       // datos: [num, num, ...]\n  var svg = document.getElementById('grafico');\n  var M = {arriba: 12, abajo: 22, izq: 56, der: 12}, W = 600, H = 220;\n  var y0 = Math.min.apply(null, datos), y1 = Math.max.apply(null, datos);\n  if (y1 - y0 < 1) { y0 -= 1; y1 += 1; }       // <- la proteccion anti-NaN\n  var x = function(i){ return M.izq + (W-M.izq-M.der) * i / Math.max(1, datos.length-1); };\n  var y = function(v){ return M.arriba + (H-M.arriba-M.abajo) * (1 - (v-y0)/(y1-y0)); };\n  var linea = datos.map(function(v,i){ return (i?'L':'M') + x(i).toFixed(1) + ',' + y(v).toFixed(1); }).join('');\n  var rejilla = '', etiquetas = '';\n  for (var k = 0; k <= 3; k++) {\n    var v = y0 + (y1-y0) * k/3, yy = y(v).toFixed(1);\n    rejilla += '<line x1=\"'+M.izq+'\" x2=\"'+(W-M.der)+'\" y1=\"'+yy+'\" y2=\"'+yy+'\" stroke=\"#e1e0d9\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>';\n    etiquetas += '<text x=\"'+(M.izq-8)+'\" y=\"'+yy+'\" dy=\"4\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#898781\">'+Math.round(v).toLocaleString('es-ES')+'</text>';\n  }\n  svg.innerHTML = rejilla + etiquetas +\n    '<path d=\"'+linea+'\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2a78d6\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>';\n}\n</script>\n\n\nRespond EXACTLY in this format:\n\nTitle: <short title>\nDescription: <one sentence>\nHTML Code:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<complete working page>\n```"}
